 then finding the average of these ratios.\n\nFor 1941, the calculation is 7,607 divided by 6,080, which gives approximately 1.25. In 1942, I'll divide 12,799 by 26,011 to get around 0.49. For 1943, I'll divide 22,282 by 72,109, resulting in roughly 0.31.\n\nI'm now computing the mean of these three ratios to determine the final answer.\n\nThe sum of the ratios is 2.053, and dividing by 3 yields 0.6843. I'll round this to four decimal places as 0.6843.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_2ce08cc1a852464aa053313b","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Explore the treasury bulletin resources to understand data structure\n- [x] Extract total net budget receipts for years 1941, 1942, 1943\n- [x] Extract total national defense budget expenditures for years 1941, 1942, 1943\n- [ ] Calculate ratio for each year (receipts / defense expenditures)\n- [ ] Calculate mean of the three ratios\n- [ ] Round to 4 decimal places and write to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
